{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551907-v20-the-taking-of-the-spirit-dark-thaumaturgy","id":1551907,"title":"[V20] The Taking of the Spirit (Dark Thaumaturgy)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-06-29T00:22:52-07:00","id":1551907,"title":"[V20] The Taking of the Spirit (Dark Thaumaturgy)","content":"Hi I'm trying to figure out how the Dark Thaumaturgy path &quot;The Taking of the Spirit&quot; (Rites of Blood page 170) works.<br /> <br /> Specifically this part<br /> .<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Once contact is made, the infernalist must engage in a contested Willpower roll against the subject (difficulty 8).<br /> <br /> If the victim accumulates more successes on this contested Willpower roll before being reduced to zero Willpower, he resists the powers of Hell. In addition, the suffering he endured hardens his mind, and this infernal path may not be used against him again a full year.<br /> <br /> If the victim is reduced to zero Willpower, he must do the vampire\u2019s bidding, not speaking, staring blankly forward, in a state much like a zombie until he has regained one dot of Willpower, as per the chart below. </div> </div> </div>Either I'm overlooking something, or there is something missing about how the victim loosing Willpower.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-29T00:52:35-07:00","id":1551909,"title":"","content":"You make a contact ( the Storyteller may require a successful Dexterity + Brawl roll ) and spend a blood point - All Dark Thaumaturgy powers, including The Taking of the Spirit, require the expenditure of a Blood Point to activate. It's not an inherent costless ability (Dark Thaumaturgy follows the same activation rules as standard Thaumaturgy: you spend 1 Blood Point each time you activate a power)<br /> Once contact is made, the infernalist must engage in a contested Willpower roll against the subject (difficulty 8).<br /> <br /> If you won this contested Willpower roll, the subject loses point of Willpower - that later &quot;regenerates&quot; by the rate on the chart<br /> If the victim accumulates more successes on this contested Willpower roll before being reduced to zero Willpower, he resists the powers of Hell. In addition, the suffering he endured hardens his mind, and this infernal path may not be used against him again a full year.<br /> <br /> So your Shang Tsung-wannabe grabs the poor schmuck, yells <b>&quot;Your Soul is Mine\u200b&quot;</b> and rolls a Will vs Will, if he wins, he drains a Willpower, then next round if the contact is still up, you can do it again or grab your victim again<br /> <br /> The blood cost and the contested roll makes it more balanced\u2014you can\u2019t just rip Willpower from anyone without risk. This also means targets with high Willpower are much harder to drain.<br /> <br /> Not the best for combat, it is more like making an army (well depending of your blood reserves) &quot;soulless zombies&quot; servants or errode slowly the willpower during a torture or a defeated/incapacitated enemy<br /> It is of course mentally scarring at best, and a horrific experience to feel your mind fades, your &quot;soul&quot; and &quot;will to live&quot; and be yourself slowly beeds away.<br /> <br /> At least that is how I interpreted this - and to be honest time to time I tend to &quot;buff it up&quot; and make it an extended contested roll, not turn based, one blood point and drain untill the victim runs out of willpower or resist, to mirror the aforementioned Shang Tsung comparison\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-29T04:04:45-07:00","id":1551912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551907-v20-the-taking-of-the-spirit-dark-thaumaturgy?p=1551909#post1551909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you won this contested Willpower roll, the subject loses point of Willpower - that later &quot;regenerates&quot; by the rate on the chart<br /> If the victim accumulates more successes on this contested Willpower roll before being reduced to zero Willpower, he resists the powers of Hell. In addition, the suffering he endured hardens his mind, and this infernal path may not be used against him again a full year.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok but how many Willpower Points does the subject loose?<br /> And i this an extended Willpower role or do need to use the power multiple times to strip the subject of it's will power?<br /> And do the successes accumlated over multiple roles or count for each role individually?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-29T04:46:28-07:00","id":1551914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aahz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551907-v20-the-taking-of-the-spirit-dark-thaumaturgy?p=1551912#post1551912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok but how many Willpower Points does the subject loose?</div> </div> </div> </div>One<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aahz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551907-v20-the-taking-of-the-spirit-dark-thaumaturgy?p=1551912#post1551912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And i this an extended Willpower role or do need to use the power multiple times to strip the subject of it's will power?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you make this as an extended contested roll, then every time you &quot;won&quot; you victim loses one willpower but you don't need to restart the power<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aahz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551907-v20-the-taking-of-the-spirit-dark-thaumaturgy?p=1551912#post1551912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And do the successes accumlated over multiple roles or count for each role individually?</div> </div> </div> </div>Individually<br /> Then again, this is just my interpretation<br /> I could be wrong, the power was worded very poorly<br /> <br /> The original version from the Revised Guide to he Sabbat book (p.101) is better:<br /> <b>System:</b> The victim loses a number of temporary Willpower equal of the vampire's mastery of this path.<br /> Should the victim know what is taking place the player my resist with her own willpower eoll (difficulity 7).<br /> If the victim's player accomulates more sucesses on this extended, resisted roll than the thaumaturge before reduced to zero Willpower, this path may not be used against her character by the same thaumaturge for a ful Year.<br /> If the victim is reduced to zero Willpower, she must do the vampire's bidding, not speaking, staring balnkly forward, i na state much like a zombie.<br /> The victim regains a Willpower point per night, which the thaumaturge may continue to try to steal away.<br /> If she sees her &quot;master&quot; killed, she regains full Willpower pool immadietly.<br /> \u200b<br /> \u2022 1 Willpower loss<br /> \u2022 \u2022 2 Willpower loss<br /> \u2022 \u2022 \u2022 4 Willpower loss<br /> \u2022 \u2022 \u2022 \u2022 6 Willpower loss<br /> \u2022 \u2022 \u2022 \u2022 \u2022 8 Willpower loss\u200b<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}